  "prefLabel": "Ins 3701.04 Objectives of Information Security Program",
  "priorExpiration": "2015-07-01",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ins 3701.04 Objectives of Information Security Program. A licensee’s information security program shall be designed to:\n\n(a) Ensure the security and confidentiality of customer information;\n\n(b) Protect against any anticipated threats or hazards to the security or integrity of the information; and\n\n(c) Protect against unauthorized access to or use of the information that could result in substantial harm or inconvenience to any customer.\n\nSource. #8901, eff 7-1-07, EXPIRED: 7-1-15\n\nNew. #11015, eff 1-8-16",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins3700.html"
